@startuml fetch_blocks_merge
title FTQ target -> ordered block bytes -> existing Decode path
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 95

legend left
  |= Prefix |= Meaning |
  | [E] | Existing gem5 call, return, or signal |
  | [N] | Proposed interface or integration hook |
  | [A] | Algorithm step / private plumbing, not a C++ method |
  Timing callbacks and stage ticks can occur in different cycles.
endlegend

participant "O3 CPU / event queue" as CPU
participant Fetch
participant FTQ
participant BlockFetchEngine as Engine
participant MergedFetchStream as Stream
participant "MMU / ITLB" as MMU
participant "FetchTranslation" as Translation
participant "Fetch::IcachePort" as Port
participant "I-cache / memory" as Cache
participant "ISA decoder" as Decoder
participant "FetchStruct time buffer" as Buffer
participant Decode

CPU -> Fetch : [E] tick() -> fetch(status_change)
Fetch -> Fetch : [E] ftqReady(tid, status_change)
Fetch -> FTQ : [E] isHeadReady(tid)
FTQ --> Fetch : [E] ready / empty or invalid
alt target ready
    Fetch -> FTQ : [E] readHead(tid)
    FTQ --> Fetch : [E] FetchTargetPtr
    Fetch -> Engine : [N] begin(ft), once for a new target
    note over Fetch, Engine
      One FTQ entry contains N ordered FetchBlocks.
      Replace legacy whole-target inRange() checks with active-block checks.
      nextQueryPC is NOT the instruction fetch address.
    end note
else no target
    Fetch -> Fetch : [E] set FtqWait; return from fetch()
end

group Repeated scheduling opportunities while this target remains live
    Fetch -> Engine : [N] nextRead()
    Engine --> Fetch : [N] optional FetchRead(tag, vaddr, size, instructionPC)
    note over Fetch, Stream
      Minimum-change mode: at most one demand request/thread in flight.
      All request sites, including pipelineIcacheAccesses(), use this cursor.
      Keep the shared retryPkt / cacheBlocked arbitration across threads.
      A block can need several fragments or reuse already buffered bytes.
      Fragment count is not necessarily the number of FetchBlocks.
    end note
    alt required bytes already buffered
        Fetch -> Engine : [N] onBytes(tag, valid cached bytes)
        Engine -> Stream : [N] append(blockIndex, fragment)
    else request permitted and no live request for this thread
        Fetch -> Fetch : [A] reserve RequestTag for this demand read
        Fetch -> Fetch : [E] fetchCacheLine(vaddr, tid, instructionPC)
        note right of Fetch
          Existing helper aligns to fetchBufferSize and reads that size.
          FetchRead.size does not silently change its three-argument API.
          Reuse aligned requests and select each fragment's valid bytes.
          Preserve cacheBlocked, interrupt, and translation guards.
        end note
        Fetch -> Fetch : [A] associate newly created RequestPtr with RequestTag
        Fetch -> MMU : [E] translateTiming(req, tc, translation, Execute)
        MMU -> Translation : [E] finish(fault, req, tc, mode)
        Translation -> Fetch : [E] finishTranslation(fault, req)
        note over MMU, Translation
          Translation can finish inline or from a later event.
          FetchTranslation deletes itself after forwarding the result.
        end note
        alt canceled request or stale translation
            Fetch -> Fetch : [E] reject mismatched status / memReq identity
            Fetch -> Fetch : [A] also validate live RequestTag after suffix recovery
        else live translation fault
            Fetch -> Engine : [N] onFault(tag, fault)
            note over Fetch, Engine
              Proposed hook buffers the fault at its stream position.
              At the oldest undecoded instruction, use the existing fault-
              carrying nop path in finishTranslation: buildInst(),
              setNotAnInst(), setPredTarg(), fault, TrapPending.
              If fetchWidth / fetchQueue capacity is unavailable,
              retain the fault and reschedule as FinishTranslationEvent does.
              Use the faulting instruction PC, not the next block's PC.
            end note
        else translated address outside physical memory
            Fetch -> Fetch : [E] set NoGoodAddr; clear memReq; await recovery
        else live successful translation
            Fetch -> Fetch : [E] create ReadReq packet; invalidate fetchBuffer
            Fetch -> Port : [E] sendTimingReq(packet)
            Port -> Cache : [E] timing request delivery
            Cache --> Port : [E] request accepted or refused
            Port --> Fetch : [E] bool accepted
            alt refused
                Fetch -> Fetch : [E] IcacheWaitRetry; save retryPkt / retryTid;
                Fetch -> Fetch : [E] cacheBlocked = true
                ... I-cache later permits retry ...
                Cache -> Port : [E] recvReqRetry()
                Port -> Fetch : [E] recvReqRetry()
                alt retry request still live
                    Fetch -> Port : [E] sendTimingReq(retryPkt)
                    Port -> Cache : [E] retry same packet
                    note over Fetch, Cache
                      Another refusal keeps the retry pending.
                      Success sets IcacheWaitResponse and clears retry state.
                    end note
                else canceled or trap pending
                    Fetch -> Fetch : [E] discard canceled retry / clear cacheBlocked
                end
            else accepted
                Fetch -> Fetch : [E] set IcacheWaitResponse; notify request probe
            end
            opt request accepted, initially or after retry
                ... response arrives as a memory timing event ...
                Cache -> Port : [E] recvTimingResp(packet)
                Port -> Fetch : [E] processCacheCompletion(packet)
                alt stale or canceled completion
                    Fetch -> Fetch : [E] reject if status / packet->req != memReq
                    Fetch -> Fetch : [A] also reject canceled RequestTag; keep surviving prefix
                    Fetch -> Fetch : [E] delete packet
                else live completion
                    Fetch -> Fetch : [E] copy bytes; fetchBufferValid = true
                    Fetch -> Engine : [N] onBytes(tag, valid fragment bytes)
                    Engine -> Stream : [N] append(blockIndex, fragment)
                    Fetch -> CPU : [E] wakeCPU()
                    Fetch -> Fetch : [E] activate; set completion/block status;
                    Fetch -> Fetch : [E] notify completion probe; delete packet; clear memReq
                end
            end
        end
    end
end

... next eligible Fetch::tick; no decoding inside memory callbacks ...
CPU -> Fetch : [E] tick() -> fetch(status_change)
Fetch -> Engine : [N] peekDecodeSlice()
Engine -> Stream : [N] peekReadyPrefix()
Stream --> Engine : [N] optional PC-tagged FetchSlice
Engine --> Fetch : [N] optional FetchSlice
alt ordered head is a translation fault
    alt fetchWidth and fetchQueue capacity available
        Fetch -> Fetch : [E] buildInst(..., faultingPC, faultingPC, false)
        Fetch -> Fetch : [E] setNotAnInst(); setPredTarg(faultingPC); attach fault
        Fetch -> Fetch : [E] set TrapPending; mark activity
        note right of Fetch
          Reuse the existing fault-carrier operations from finishTranslation.
          Their emission is newly gated by ordered stream readiness.
          Younger faulting blocks cannot overtake older instructions.
        end note
    else capacity unavailable
        Fetch -> Fetch : [A] retain head fault; retry on an eligible stage/event
    end
else ready bytes at predicted execution head
    Fetch -> Decoder : [E] moreBytesPtr() / moreBytes(realPC, fetchAddr)
    Fetch -> Decoder : [E] instReady(); decode(realPC)
    Decoder --> Fetch : [E] StaticInst (or request more contiguous bytes)
    ref over Fetch, Engine, Decoder
      predecode_feedback.puml:
      buildInst -> BAC::updatePC -> bridge / IBPU binding -> cursor advance
    end ref
    note over Engine, Decoder
      Decode the ready prefix without waiting for every block.
      Merge order is block order, not address order.
      Example: 0x1000..0x100c, then 0x8000..0x800c.
      Each DynInst retains its real PC; do not fetch the intervening gap.
      Join partial instructions only across contiguous fragments.
      Never join a partial instruction across a taken discontinuity.
    end note
else head bytes not ready
    Fetch -> Fetch : [A] stop this decode attempt; retain target/cursor
end

group Tail of the same Fetch::tick
    opt issuePipelinedIfetch[tid]
        Fetch -> Fetch : [E] pipelineIcacheAccesses(tid)
        Fetch -> Engine : [N] nextRead() instead of legacy next-PC arithmetic
        note right of Fetch
          Route an eligible read through the same request path above.
          Do not create a second requester beside BlockFetchEngine.
        end note
    end
    loop up to decodeWidth, with per-thread Decode stalls respected
        Fetch -> Fetch : [E] select fetchQueue[tid].front()
        Fetch -> Buffer : [E] write toDecode->insts[toDecode->size++]
        Fetch -> Fetch : [E] fetchQueue[tid].pop_front()
    end
end
... configured fetchToDecodeDelay, via the stage time buffer ...
CPU -> Decode : [E] tick()
Decode -> Buffer : [E] sortInsts() reads fromFetch at -fetchToDecodeDelay
note over Buffer, Decode
  This is delayed data delivery, not a direct Fetch::decode() call.
  ISA byte decoding already occurred in Fetch.
end note

note over Fetch, Cache
  Existing anchors: src/cpu/o3/fetch.cc
  ftqReady:513; fetchCacheLine:529; finishTranslation:578;
  processCacheCompletion:356; fetch:1058; tick:821;
  recvReqRetry:1403; pipelineIcacheAccesses:1574;
  IcachePort callbacks:1658,1670.
  fetch.hh: FetchTranslation::finish:119, FinishTranslationEvent::process:149.
  decode.cc: setFetchQueue:212, sortInsts:484.
end note
@enduml
